James sought an efficient way to manage citations in Google Docs without using a citation manager, expressing concern over time lost while formatting citations. Arachne provided a structured approach, including creating a consistent reference format, utilizing Google Docs tools (like the Find feature), and establishing a cross-check list of citations. Arachne suggested manual checkpoints for final verification and utilizing comments for clarity in collaborations. Lastly, she mentioned the possibility of automating checks with a script for those with minimal programming skills. This guidance aimed to streamline citation management while maintaining consistency and accuracy.
